{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The first of your dough.</b> When you knead the dough you are accustomed to knead in the wilderness — and how much is it? ״וַיָּמֹדּוּ בָעֹמֶר״ (Exodus 16), ״עֹמֶר לַגֻּלְגֹּלֶת״ (ibid.) — you shall lift from its first, i.e., before you eat of it; the first of its portion — <b>one loaf</b> — <b>you shall lift as a gift</b> to the name of YHWH (Eruvin 3)." "<b>A loaf.</b> טורטי״ל בְּלַעַז." "<b>Like the gift of the threshing floor.</b> For no measure was stated for it, unlike the gift of tithe, for which a measure was stated (Sifrei). But the Sages gave a measure — for a householder, one out of twenty-four, and for a baker, one out of forty-eight (Ḥallah 2)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French tortel, a round loaf."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:04.845385697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}